  "badge": {
    "id": "escort",
    "name": "Escort"
  },
  "briefing": {
    "situation": "Four B-17s are bombing the hangars at Dulag, the Japanese strip fifteen miles southwest, from ten thousand feet. You are their escort: stay with them. Zeros will come up to meet the formation, and at least three bombers must reach the target and bomb it. Their gunners will help, but they cannot hold off fighters on their own. Recover at Tacloban once the bombs are down.",
    "loadout": "clean"
  },
  "history": {
    "text": "In the last months of 1944 the heavy bombers of the Army's Far East Air Forces struck Japanese airfields across the Philippines, with fighters along to keep the interceptors off them. This mission is inspired by those raids rather than a reconstruction of any one of them. By then the theater's heavy bombers were B-24 Liberators, which this game does not have, so B-17s stand in; Navy Hellcats did not normally escort Army bombers; and Dulag, the Japanese strip here as in Airfield Strike, was in American hands within days of the landing on 20 October 1944.",
    "sources": [
      "Wesley Frank Craven and James Lea Cate, eds., \"The Army Air Forces in World War II\", Volume V, \"The Pacific: Matterhorn to Nagasaki\" (Office of Air Force History, 1953): https://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/AAF/V/index.html",
      "M. Hamlin Cannon, \"Leyte: The Return to the Philippines\" (United States Army in World War II, Office of the Chief of Military History, 1954): https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/48991"
    ]
  }
